.TH QLEVER\-UI\-DEPLOY 7 "2026-03-30" "qlever-ui-deploy" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
qlever\-ui\-deploy \- production deployment configuration for qlever\-ui
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B qlever\-ui\-deploy
package provides the configuration files needed to run
.BR qlever\-ui (1)
as a production service:
.IP \(bu 2
A
.BR systemd (1)
socket unit and service unit that start
.B gunicorn
listening on a Unix domain socket.
.IP \(bu
A ready-to-use
.BR nginx (8)
virtual-host configuration.
.IP \(bu
A ready-to-use
.BR apache2 (8)
virtual-host configuration.
.PP
After installation the service is not yet started or enabled.
Follow the steps below to bring it up.
.SH QUICK START
Enable and start the socket and service:
.PP
.EX
systemctl enable \-\-now qlever\-ui.socket
systemctl enable \-\-now qlever\-ui.service
.EE
.PP
Verify the service is running:
.PP
.EX
systemctl status qlever\-ui.service
.EE
.PP
The gunicorn process now listens on the Unix socket
.IR /run/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.sock .
Use one of the reverse-proxy configurations below to expose it over HTTP,
or see
.B DIRECT TCP EXPOSURE
to bind to a TCP port instead.
.SH NGINX
The package installs an nginx virtual-host configuration at
.IR /etc/nginx/sites\-available/qlever\-ui .
It listens on port
.B 8176
and proxies all requests to the Unix socket.
Static files are served directly from
.IR /usr/share/qlever\-ui/static/ .
.PP
Enable the site and reload nginx:
.PP
.EX
ln \-s /etc/nginx/sites\-available/qlever\-ui \e
      /etc/nginx/sites\-enabled/qlever\-ui
nginx \-t && systemctl reload nginx
.EE
.PP
The UI is then reachable at
.IR http://<host>:8176/ .
.PP
The
.B www\-data
user is added to the
.B qlever\-ui
group during package installation so that nginx can read the socket.
If nginx is installed after
.B qlever\-ui\-deploy
you may need to add
.B www\-data
to the group manually:
.PP
.EX
usermod \-aG qlever\-ui www\-data
.EE
.SH APACHE
The package installs an Apache virtual-host configuration at
.IR /etc/apache2/sites\-available/qlever\-ui.conf .
It listens on port
.B 8176
and proxies all requests to the Unix socket via
.BR mod_proxy .
Static files are served directly from
.IR /usr/share/qlever\-ui/static/ .
.PP
Enable the required modules and the site, then reload Apache:
.PP
.EX
a2enmod proxy proxy_http headers
a2ensite qlever\-ui
systemctl reload apache2
.EE
.PP
The UI is then reachable at
.IR http://<host>:8176/ .
.PP
Apache's
.B www\-data
user must be a member of the
.B qlever\-ui
group to access the socket (see the note in the
.B NGINX
section above).
.PP
.B Note:
Port 8176 is not in Apache's default
.I ports.conf
listen list.
Add
.B Listen 8176
to
.I /etc/apache2/ports.conf
if Apache does not already listen on that port.
.SH DIRECT TCP EXPOSURE
By default the service binds to a Unix socket so that only a local reverse
proxy can reach it.
To expose the service directly on a TCP port — for example on a machine
without nginx or Apache — override the service unit.
.PP
Create a systemd drop-in:
.PP
.EX
systemctl edit qlever\-ui.service
.EE
.PP
Add the following lines to the editor that opens
.RI ( /etc/systemd/system/qlever\-ui.service.d/override.conf ):
.PP
.EX
[Unit]
After=network.target
Requires=

[Service]
ExecStart=
ExecStart=/opt/venvs/qlever\-ui/bin/gunicorn \e
    qlever.wsgi:application \e
    \-\-bind 0.0.0.0:8176 \e
    \-\-workers 4 \e
    \-\-timeout 120 \e
    \-\-access\-logfile /var/log/qlever\-ui/access.log \e
    \-\-error\-logfile /var/log/qlever\-ui/error.log \e
    \-\-limit\-request\-line 10000
.EE
.PP
Apply the changes:
.PP
.EX
systemctl daemon\-reload
systemctl restart qlever\-ui.service
.EE
.PP
The UI is then reachable at
.IR http://<host>:8176/ .
The
.B qlever\-ui.socket
unit is no longer used and can be stopped and disabled:
.PP
.EX
systemctl disable \-\-now qlever\-ui.socket
.EE
.PP
.B Security note:
When binding directly on TCP the service is reachable by any client that can
connect to port 8176.
Restrict access with a firewall if the port should not be publicly reachable.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Runtime configuration is stored in
.IR /etc/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.env .
This file is created during package installation and is readable only by
.B root
and members of the
.B qlever\-ui
group.
Restart the service after making changes:
.PP
.EX
systemctl restart qlever\-ui.service
.EE
.PP
Before exposing the service externally, at minimum update
.B QLEVERUI_ALLOWED_HOSTS
and
.B QLEVERUI_CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS
in
.IR /etc/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.env
to reflect the public hostname.
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_SECRET_KEY
Django secret key.
A secure random value is generated automatically at install time.
Do not share or commit this value.
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_DEBUG
Enable Django debug mode.
Default:
.IR False .
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_ALLOWED_HOSTS
Comma-separated list of hostnames Django will serve.
Must include the public hostname when the service is exposed externally.
Default:
.IR localhost .
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS
Comma-separated list of trusted origins for CSRF protection.
Must include the scheme and hostname, e.g.\&
.IR https://qlever.example.com .
Default:
.IR http://localhost .
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_DATABASE_URL
Database URL in
.B django\-environ
format.
Default:
.IR sqlite:////var/lib/qlever\-ui/qleverui.sqlite3 .
.TP
.B QLEVERUI_STATIC_ROOT
Directory from which static files are served.
Default:
.IR /usr/share/qlever\-ui/static .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.env
Runtime configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/nginx/sites\-available/qlever\-ui
nginx virtual-host configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/apache2/sites\-available/qlever\-ui.conf
Apache virtual-host configuration.
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/qlever\-ui.service
Systemd service unit (gunicorn).
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/qlever\-ui.socket
Systemd socket unit.
.TP
.I /run/qlever\-ui/qlever\-ui.sock
Unix domain socket (created at runtime).
.TP
.I /var/lib/qlever\-ui/qleverui.sqlite3
Application database.
.TP
.I /var/log/qlever\-ui/access.log
Gunicorn access log.
.TP
.I /var/log/qlever\-ui/error.log
Gunicorn error log.
.TP
.I /usr/share/qlever\-ui/static/
Static files served directly by the web server.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qlever\-ui (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR nginx (8),
.BR apache2 (8)
